{"availability":"available","full":"roboflow/trackers","name":"trackers","description":"Trackers gives you clean, modular re-implementations of leading multi-object tracking algorithms released under the permissive Apache 2.0 license. You combine them with any detection model you already use.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":3903,"forks":417,"created":"2025-04-14T16:12:26Z","updated":"2026-10-03T23:35:00Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"develop","homepage":"https://trackers.roboflow.com/","topics":["bot-sort","bytetrack","dancetrack","mot17","multi-object-tracking","oc-sort","soccernet","sort","sportsmot","trackeval"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/roboflow/trackers","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:27.736Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:27.736Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:27.736Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:11:27.736Z","stars":3903,"forks":417}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Plug-and-play object tracking in Python (multi-object) for any detection model.","trackers is an object tracking library for Python. It gives you clean-room, benchmarked implementations of SORT, ByteTrack, OC-SORT, BoT-SORT, C-BIoU, and McByte — so occlusions, fast motion, and moving cameras stop being your problem to solve from scratch. It speaks supervision.Detections natively, slotting into any detector you already use — YOLO, DETR, RT-DETR, or anything else — without glue code. One consistent interface, whether you're a researcher comparing algorithms, an engineer shipping a production pipeline, or a hobbyist building something cool. Requires Python ≥ 3.10."],"features":["Clean-room implementations. Every algorithm is re-implemented from the original paper — not vendored or wrapped. You can read it, understand it, and modify it.","Apache 2.0, no copyleft. Ship it inside closed-source products — unlike AGPL-3.0 alternatives such as BoxMOT.","Detector-agnostic. Works with YOLO, DETR, RT-DETR, or any model that produces bounding boxes. No inference library required or assumed.","supervision.Detections native. Plugs directly into the supervision ecosystem. Pass detections in, get tracked detections back — zero glue code.","Benchmarked across four datasets. MOT17, SportsMOT, SoccerNet, and DanceTrack — at default parameters and after hyperparameter tuning (McByte: defaults only, by design), so you know what to expect before you deploy."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/roboflow/trackers/blob/develop/README.md","fingerprint":"3780e905f43c79684ee2f8c8b291269fc16c6c50a5af7e9a31f70f1aee53a28f","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:55.185Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:55.185Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Plug-and-play object tracking in Python (multi-object) for any detection model.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/roboflow/trackers/blob/develop/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3780e905f43c79684ee2f8c8b291269fc16c6c50a5af7e9a31f70f1aee53a28f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/roboflow/trackers/blob/develop/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:55.185Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T23:35:00Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/roboflow/trackers/blob/develop/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:55.186Z","hash":"3780e905f43c79684ee2f8c8b291269fc16c6c50a5af7e9a31f70f1aee53a28f","originalBytes":12288,"storedBytes":12288,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["trackers","tracking","see","detections","hota","guide","install","mot17","tracker","algorithms","download","detector","mcbyte","sportsmot","val","annotations","any","bash","inference","license","model","motion","python","detection","evaluation","frame","get","import","one","only","pip","pipeline","test","track","benchmark","bot-sort","building","bytetrack","cli","code.","dancetrack","default","fast","four","frames","full","library","matching","numbers","options","paper","parameters"